SH(1)

NAME
    sh - BusyBox ash command interpreter

SYNOPSIS
    sh [options] [script [arg ...]]
    sh -c command

DESCRIPTION
    /bin/sh is a SmallOS launcher that execs /usr/bin/busybox sh. It exists for
    script-style POSIX compatibility and for BusyBox applets that expect a
    standard sh path.

    /bin/shell remains the native interactive SmallOS shell launched at boot.
    Use shell when you want the native command prompt, job table, and selftest
    built-ins. Use sh when a Unix script or applet expects BusyBox ash. Ash has
    basic job-control support using SmallOS process groups, Ctrl+Z stopped
    jobs, fg/bg, and waitpid WUNTRACED reporting.

EXAMPLES
    sh -c 'echo ok'
    sh -c 'grep root /etc/passwd'

SEE ALSO
    busybox(1), shell(1)
